Digital is changing the VAX 4000 Model 500A, 600A, and 700A product family
to provide more powerful systems needed to drive users' increasingly complex
databases and growing PC LANs.

VAX 4000 Model 505A

The VAX 4000 Model 505A achieves an impressive 185 TPS for a 59 percent
performance improvement over the Model 500A. Another key difference between
these two systems is price/performance: the Model 505A provides 600A
performance at about the same price as that of the 500A.

VAX 4000 Model 705A

The highest performing member of the VAX 4000 family runs at an estimated
280 TPS and 45 VUPS. Like all VAX 4000 pedestals, it includes two on-board
high speed DSSI controllers, with an option for two additional DSSI
controllers. Besides configuring with RF drives, each controller now can be
connected to the recently announced HSD05 DSSI-to-SCSI controllers. Thus all
of Digital's industry standard SCSI devices are available for VAX 4000
systems.

