For further product information, consult the August supplement of the
Systems and Options Catalog.

RACKMOUNT SYSTEMS

The new VAX 4000 Model 505A and 705A systems are available in rackmount
configurations identical in design and functionality to previous rackmount
VAX 4000 systems. Rackmounting provides a cost effective way to organize
systems, storage, and other options in one easily accessible, 19-inch-wide
EIA rackmount cabinet and thus in a small footprint. Rackmount Models 505A
and 705A require only 14 inches of vertical rack, cabinet, or enclosure
space and support the two additional high speed DSSI controllers and/or the
new HSD05 DSSI-to-SCSI controllers.

UPGRADES

The VAX 4000 family offers multiple upgrade paths to preserve users'
investments in systems, storage, and other options:

o  In-cabinet upgrades -- These are board upgrades from previous VAX 4000
   systems and include a simple swap of the CPU. (See the AVAILABILITY AND
   ORDERING section.)

o  Installed base ADVANTAGE-UPGRADES to the VAX 4000 Model 505A and 705A
   systems -- These provide easy, single-order-number upgrades from MicroVAX
   3300 to 3900 and VAX 4000 Model 200 systems.

SCSI STORAGE

Digital continues to meet user requirements for SCSI disks, tapes, and
CDROMs on all VAX 4000 systems. With the newly released HSD05 DSSI-to-SCSI
controllers, users now can use Digital industry standard SCSI devices both
internally (in the system enclosure) and externally. See the "StorageWorks
HSDO5 Array Controller" article in the March 14, 1994, issue of Digital's
Customer Update.

OpenVMS SUPPORT

Models 505A and 705A are supported in OpenVMS VAX V5.5-2H4 and V6.1. Support
