DCE V1.3 for DEC OSF/1 Systems Includes Distributed File Service

HIGHLIGHTS

o  Provides complete Distributed File Service environment for DEC OSF/1
   systems

o  Supports DEC OSF/1 V3.0 operating system and runs in a SMP configuration

o  Provides improved performance through the use of local file caching

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

DCE (Distributed Computing Environment) V1.3 for DEC OSF/1 systems offers a
single integrated file system, the DCE Distributed File Service, that is
shared among all DCE users and host computers in a DCE cell. The syntax for
moving around in the directory is UNIX like regardless of the local host
operating system. Users have have their own local directory in the file
system and use the same interface to move around in it. Consequently,
sharing files is easy. Files can be protected by the DCE software security
authentication and authorization functions. Also, files are accessible, on a
controlled basis to anyone needing access, while access is limited to other
users.

The DCE Distributed File Service, providing client and server software with
authenticated access, is integrated into the DCE Runtime Services product.
The Distributed File Service provides a unified, globally distributed file
system with all DCE Distributed File Service files accessible from any DCE
Distributed File Service machine. Every user on the network accesses a given
Distributed File Service file by the same file name, regardless of which
Distributed File Service server is storing the file. This product uses DCE
technology (security, name services, remote procedure calls, and
synchronized time) to provide access to file system services over a network.
The software also offers advanced caching to minimize the adverse
performance impact of network operations and token management to allow
reliable, concurrent accesses to data.

The operation and management of DCE Distributed File Service are built upon
the DCE remote procedure calls. DCE naming services allow clients to access
files without knowing which server stores the data. The use of DCE security
services protects data against unauthorized use and provides for the
authentication of access requests.

This product for DEC OSF/1 is a port of the OSF V1.0.3a Distributed File
Service technology to 64-bit, SMP-safe DEC OSF/1 V3.0, improving the quality
and performance. Although the OSF DCE technology includes the Episode file
system technology, the Distributed File Service set of codes will replace
Episode with the the POLYCENTER Advanced File System.

This release of DCE Distributed File Service is an implementation of the
Distributed File Service Executive Services capability. Future releases will
expand this capability to include Distributed File Service Enhanced
Services, such as:

o  File replication
o  File migration
o  Online backup
o  Enhanced recovery capabilities
o  Enhanced administration capabilities

BENEFITS

o  Provides a set of services to allow easy development of distributed
   client/server applications.

o  Supplies consistent set of distributed services that interoperate across
   heterogeneous platforms.

o  Offers increased application portability through the use of consistent
   APIs across multivendor platforms.

o  Provides transparent, global access to files.

o  Improves performance through the use of local file caching.

o  Offers faster recovery from failures with the POLYCENTER Advanced File
   System as the local file system.

o  Offers full concurrent file usage and single site semantics.

o  Full DCE services across a range of open platforms, including DEC OSF/1,
   OpenVMS, Windows NT, and Windows 3.1 environments.

o  Comprehensive consulting capability on DCE based distributed application
   development. This includes initial evaluation, application prototyping,
   and full application design consulting and systems integration.

o  Ease of use and management improvements that greatly simplify the
   development and deployment of DCE applications.

AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING

DCE V1.3 for DEC OSF/1 systems will be available in September 1994. The DCE
Distributed File Service, providing client/server software with
authenticated access, is integrated into the DCE Runtime Services kit. There
is no additional license fee for this additional capability.

The documentation sets for DCE Runtime Services, DCE Cell Directory Server,
and DCE Security Server are identical. Users need to purchase only one.

