TECHNICAL DATA

Performance

o  Forwarding rate: 6,000 packets per second (parameter dependent).
o  Filtering rate: 13,000 packets per second.

Manageability

o  SNMP network management for configuration and maintenance.
o  Implements SNMP's MIB-II support for dumping RIP routing tables, enabling
   enhanced troubleshooting of network problems.
o  Can be managed in-band, over the network, or from a local EIA RS232
   console port.

Cable TV Features

o  Supports distances of up to 70 miles, roundtrip, from the head end.
o  Supports bidirectional, single and dual cable plants.
o  Frequency agile across frequency range of 10 to 550 MHz.
o  Operates in any available 6 MHz channel.

Security

The ChannelWorks portfolio provides a security group feature that allows
multiple users to share the same RF channel while operating as if they are
on different networks.

A secure ChannelWorks network is provided via features such as IP address
filtering, traffic type filtering, and broadcast and route filtering.

Built-in security features prevent tampering with the cable TV receive and
transmit frequencies.

RF Electrical Specifications

o  Signalling rate: 10 Mbps.
o  Modulation: quadrature phase shift keying.
o  Spectral efficiency: 1.67 bits/Hz.

Transmitter

o  Minimum frequency range: 10 to 174 MHz.
o  Bandwidth: < 6 MHz.

Receiver

o  Minimum frequency range: 54 to 550 MHz.
o  BER @ 25 dB C/N: <1 in 10 to the 9th power.

Installation

o  Desktop, rackmount, and wallmount.
o  Single cable plant requires a frequency translator.

Physical Dimensions

o  Length: 11.5 inches.
o  Width: 11.5 inches.
o  Height: 3.47 inches.
o  Weight: 12 lb.


