MULTIMEDIA SERVICES V1.2 FOR DEC OSF/1 AXP

Highlights:

o  Software JPEG decompression and video screen saver part of Multimedia
   Services runtime environment on all DEC OSF/1 AXP DEC 3000 workstations

o  Support for video output on Sound and Motion J300 TURBOchannel option and
   two boards on one system

Product Description:

Multimedia Services V1.2 for DEC OSF/1 AXP systems (SPD 48.92.02) is a
runtime and programming environment bringing audio and video capabilities to
Digital's workstations. It provides support for the built-in audio on
Digital's Alpha AXP workstations running the DEC OSF/1 operating system, the
Sound and Motion J300 TURBOchannel multimedia option, and the Microsoft
Windows Sound System, plus a full programming library for use by developers.

The application programming interface (API) is based on the same multimedia
interface provided in Microsoft's Windows NT and Windows 3.1 operating
systems, giving Digital a common multimedia environment across three of the
leading industry platforms.

The new features in the V1.2 release include:

o  Support for software JPEG decompression, allowing Motion JPEG AVI files
   to be played on an Alpha AXP workstation without requiring the Sound and
   Motion J300 card. This feature is supported through the API, the playback
   utility, and the video screen saver.

   The playback performance is highly dependent on the performance of the
   Alpha AXP processor. Thus, a 320 x 240 Motion JPEG file is displayed at 6
   to 15 frames per second.

o  Video screen saver that displays motion JPEG AVI files -- and the power
   of Alpha AXP systems.

o  Support for two Sound and Motion J300 options in one system, allowing two
   simultaneous video input sources.

o  Video output support through the Sound and Motion J300 option to transfer
   anything displayed on the workstation monitor (including graphics, video,
   and text) to a video output device such as a VCR or television monitor.

Benefits:

With the performance of the Alpha AXP processor, video can be displayed in
software only, continuing the movement to complete multimedia integration in
Alpha AXP systems. Software video can be used in areas such as video
documentation, presentations, and video conferencing.

Availability and Ordering:

Multimedia Services V1.2 for DEC OSF/1 AXP systems is available now. Media
are distributed on the Layered Products CDROM for DEC OSF/1 software. A
Multimedia Services runtime license is included with all DEC OSF/1 AXP
workstations, and the runtime software is factory installed on prepackaged
systems. (Users with systems ordered before October 1993 need to order a
license.)

