DIGITAL AND MICROSOFT COM DESIGN REVIEW

On July 15, 1994, Digital and Microsoft hosted a detailed technical review
of the preliminary common object model (COM) specification with users,
system integrators, and system vendors. Feedback from the design review will
be used to modify the preliminary specification.

A phased adoption plan for users interested in COM was outlined. The first
phase involves making use of the distributed OLE capabilities inherent in
ObjectBroker V2.5, followed by design planning based on the COM
specification, piloting based upon an advanced developers' kit, and full
deployment. Microsoft will begin shipping COM in its operating systems
starting with Cairo. Digital will begin shipping COM in ObjectBroker
software, with full implementation scheduled for V3.0.

