 DIGITAL FOCUSES ON THE INTERNET - ANNOUNCES THE INTERNET BUSINESS
 GROUP......Digital has formally announced the creation of the Internet
 Business Group (IBG), bringing a focused commitment to the Internet
 market. Headed by Vice President, Rose Ann Giordano, the new group will
 work closely with existing organizations that already provide Internet
 solutions for customers. Digital was the first computer company in the
 industry to utilize the World-Wide Web, ensuring marketing information
 was readily available to its customers; has created one of the world's
 best Internet security, offering Screening External Access Link,
 (S.E.A.L.), and uses the Internet as a channel for direct sales through
 Digital's Electronic Connection. The new Internet Business Group will
 continue the company's focus on providing innovative ways of utilizing
 the Internet technology to meet the needs of customers and partners.

 CHANNELWORKS INTERNET BROUTER FOR HIGH-SPEED INTERNET ACCESS....Digital
 has announced the ChannelWorks Internet Brouter, a product that allows
 high-speed access to the Internet over standard cable television
 systems. The ChannelWorks Internet Brouter provides inexpensive access
 to and routing of Internet traffic, at significantly greater speeds
 than those of traditional leased lines. It allows ChannelWorks users to
 access worldwide databases and information repositories such as the
 World-Wide Web and WAIS (Wide Area Information Servers). Use of the
 ChannelWorks technology for school networking is being tested by the
 University of Pittsburgh, the Pittsburgh Supercomputing Center, and the
 Pittsburgh Public Schools in a project entitled "Common Knowledge:
 Pittsburgh". Robert Carlitz, Professor of Physics at the University of
 Pittsburgh states, "Digital's ChannelWorks technology offers what may
 be an optimal solution to school connectivity, with the promise of high
 bandwidth at moderate prices".

 * ChannelWorks Brouter Info Sheet; news0801.txt;

 DIGITAL ANNOUNCES FASTEST AXP WORKSTATIONS.......Digital has announced
 two new workstations, the DEC 3000 Models 700 and 900 AXP, offering
 customers the best combination of price and 2D and 3D graphics
 performance. Both workstations run DEC OSF/1, Digital's standards-
 compliant UNIX, and OpenVMS operating systems. The Model 700 handles
 large applications such as 2D and 3D mechanical computer-aided design
 (MCAD), electronic design automation (EDA), scientific visualization,
 and high-end financial modeling. The Model 900 excels at complex
 applications in structural engineering, computational fluid dynamics,
 structural biology, and condensed matter physics. Users can run complex
 technical, business, and scientific applications right from their
 workstations with quicker response and faster turnaround, leaving them
 more time to develop new designs, run more simulations or improve
 existing models.

 * New Alpha AXP Workstations Press Release; news0802.txt;
 * DEC 3000 Model 700 Info Sheet; news0803.txt;
 * DEC 3000 Model 900 Info Sheet; news0804.txt;

 NEW ADVANTAGECLUSTER COMPUTE SERVER 5000 ANNOUNCED........Digital has
 announced the new AdvantageCluster Compute Server 5000 system which
 features high-performance UNIX clustering capability with SMP support.
 The new system provides an economical solution for such applications as
 complex process simulation, computational fluid dynamics, and financial
 modeling. It consists of four Digital 2100 Model A500MP systems
 packaged in a single enclosure creating a cost-effective, high-powered
 alternative to costly supercomputing systems in networked UNIX
 environments. The processors in the AdvantageCluster Compute Server
 5000 system are two to five times more powerful than processors in
 traditional massively parallel processor (MPP) systems.

 * New AdvantageCluster Compute Server Press Release; news0802.txt;

 DIGITAL'S OSF/1 RATED AS MOST STANDARD.......A recent study from D.H.
 Brown Associates rated DEC OSF/1 as the most standard operating system
 on the market. For open systems, DEC OSF/1 V2.0 was first with a 92%
 conformance to standards. The comparison rated 20 different operating
 systems, including IBM and HP. Digital's OpenVMS operating system was
 the first non-UNIX system, placing 7th overall with a 74% conformance
 to standards.

 U.S. CSLG PROGRAM ANNOUNCES PAKS ON CDROM.....Beginning August 5, 1994,
 Digital will ship all Campuswide Software License Grant (CSLG) Product
 Authorization Keys (PAKs) on CDROM media only. This change is a result
 of customer feedback received on the program. Effectively CSLG PAKs
 will no longer be shipped on TK50, Magtape, or paper. All the CSLG
 portfolios will be combined on the same CDROM and orderable under one
 new part number. The fee for the CSLG PAK CDROM is $500. Updated CSLG
 PAK CDROM's may be purchased on a quarterly basis once the prerequisite
 annual membership fee has been paid. Included on the CSLG PAK CDROM
 will be products for OpenVMS, ULTRIX, DEC OSF/1, DOS, OS/2, Windows,
 MACINTOSH, SUN, and Windows NT (new).

 DIGITAL AND ORACLE ANNOUNCE WORLDWIDE ENTERPRISE SOLUTIONS PROGRAM.....
 Digital and Oracle Corporation have announced the launch of the
 Enterprise Solutions Program (ESP), a worldwide initiative offering a
 complete suite of products and services to customers seeking mainframe
 alternatives. The program is intended to provide better solutions for
 decision support applications that can benefit from moving to an open
 relational database environment. With this initiative in place, Digital
 and Oracle will enable customers to obtain their products, consulting
 services, and support through a single contact. The rollout of this
 program will begin with a small set of key customers in the second half
 of calendar year 1994 and deliver products and services to the general
 market in 1995.

 * Digital and Oracle ESP Press Release; news0805.txt;

 DIGITAL INTRODUCES DECTALK EXPRESS SPEECH SYNTHESIZER.....Digital has
 introduced DECtalk Express Speech Synthesizer, a portable speech
 synthesis product providing expanded PC capabilities for individuals
 who are blind, visually impaired, or have learning disabilities. The
 DECtalk Express Speech Synthesizer converts ASCII text to synthesized
 speech output, allowing users to hear computer monitor screen contents,
 database contents and other text, communicated via natural-sounding
 DECtalk speech. The product provides users access to a wide range of
 computer applications, including word processing, electronic mail,
 spread-sheets, and database applications. The DECtalk Express Speech
 Synthesizer may also be used for text-to-speech applications in
 education.

 * DECtalk Express Speech Synthesizer Info Sheet; news0806.txt;

 WIDE AREA NETWORK SUPPORT ANNOUNCED FOR OPENVMS CLUSTERS.....Multi-site
 OpenVMS Cluster configurations, a new feature of both VMScluster and
 VAXcluster software, enable users to operate systems as far apart as
 150 miles as a single OpenVMS Cluster unit. The support of DS3 (or T3)
 technology makes this possible. The combination of cluster functional-
 ity and WAN distances gives users a more cost effective way to run
 their institutions, and provides 100 percent data integrity at each
 site upon completion of each individual transaction. It allows users at
 one site immediate local access to the latest data, even if it has just
 been updated by users at another site. Instead of requiring support
 staff at multiple locations, users will need fewer staff to manage
 their multisite OpenVMS Cluster system, freeing up personnel for other
 MIS activities and end-user services.

 * WAN Support for OpenVMS Clusters Info Sheet; news0807.txt;

