 ALPHA AXP'S "STELLAR" PERFORMANCE AT UNIVERSITY OF LONDON......Using
 Digital's Alpha AXP computers to give accurate visualizations of
 stellar activity, the University of London's Mullard Space Science
 Laboratory (MSSL), in London, England has gathered new information to
 help explain the physical behavior of the star systems and the sun.
 Scientists at the laboratory are using an Alpha AXP DEC 3000 Model 400
 workstation to run a computer model to evaluate unusual X-ray emissions
 from a binary star system. Using data processed on the computer to
 develop a complex computer graphic, researchers have made some
 interesting discoveries. The detailed, computer-intensive research
 being carried out by the MSSL team was impossible on previous work-
 stations because they were too slow. Now, the researchers hope to
 refine and adapt their computer model for a range of star evaluation
 projects.

