 PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

 Users are requiring higher levels of performance, at lower costs, for
 their technical and financial applications. Digital is responding to
 these requirements with the DEC 3000 Model 700 AXP workstation,
 offering better performance than HP, Sun, and IBM systems for as little
 as half the price. In fact, the Model 700 offers more performance than
 any other desktop workstation from another vendor and it starts at only
 $23,000 for a 64 Mbyte building block and $27,698 for a system with a
 21 inch color monitor, 64 Mbyte memory, 1 Gbyte disk, and CDROM.

 Now the repriced Model 600 is the fastest workstation under $20,000
 from any vendor.

 BENEFITS

 o  As economic, business, and scientific models have become larger and
    more complex, they have exceeded the address limits of 32 bit
    hardware, requiring slower, multistep access or the use of 64 bit
    computers. Digital's Alpha AXP systems have full 64 bit
    architectures and 64 bit operating systems and can handle increasing
    demands well into the next century.

 o  DEC 3000 systems running such applications as MCAD, ECAD, GIS, and
    scientific visualization allow them to solve the larger problems
    they are now required to handle.

 o  Digital's price/performance leadership results in cost savings for
    its users, while upgrades from current Alpha AXP workstations to the
    new Model 700 protect their investment.

 AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING

 The DEC 3000 Model 700 will be available in August 1994 with DEC OSF/1
 AXP V2.1 and OpenVMS AXP V6.1.

 Digital is offering upgrades from the Model 600 family to the new Model
 700 family with a field service installed board swap. Users upgrading
 from a Model 400 will receive a complete new system box via the
 ADVANTAGE-UPGRADE program.

 Factory installed software is not a substitute for media and
 documentation. Users order either the OpenVMS AXP V6.1 or DEC OSF/1 AXP
 V2.1 media and documentation kit as a separate line item. Although all
 systems with a disk have factory installed software, we recommend at
 least one media and documentation kit per site.

 For compute intensive applications requiring more than single processor
 performance, these systems can be combined into Alpha AXP UNIX clusters
 using LSF compute share software.

 SERVICES

 DEC 3000 AXP systems are supported worldwide by Digital's service
 organization and covered by Digital's standard warranty services.

